CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 18
Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is fast, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and
j. the right to a sense of security and protection.

Article 8
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 7, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population administration and civil registration;
f. women's empowerment, protection of women and children;
g. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises; and
h. public tranquility, public order, and community protection.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 23
(1) The Regional Government develops cooperation patterns for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
